  "summary": "A specialized embroidery tradition focused on creating elaborate patterns on Agbada robes for social status and ceremonial purposes.",
  "description": "Agbada embroidery features intricate geometric and symbolic patterns stitched with metallic threads, silk, or cotton onto wide-sleeved robes. This embroidery tradition developed as a visual language of social status among Yoruba nobility and has evolved into a significant economic sector supporting specialized artisans.",
